Current SDK uses only built-in Node.js APIs and Android shell tools at runtime;
those runtimes are not bundled. Importing lab fonts/icons/pet/third-party source
requires per-file provenance and retained notices in their owning module.
Source links verified 2026-10-10; external pages may change.

Local visual palette references user-provided Agentroid OS design-system v0.1
tokens (canvas ECEEF0, sage BFD0C2, charcoal 252525, primary text 121412).
The project is named Taku OS. No screenshot or reference-video assets copied.

Imported original Android runtime code is now in system/assistant, system/display,
system/overlay, tooling/app-kit and adapters/codex-runtime (source moved once).
Google Material Design Icons retain Apache-2.0: system/assistant/licenses/.
Doto retains SIL OFL-1.1: system/assistant/licenses/Doto-OFL.txt.
Desktop pet PNG sprites were Image Gen-generated from the user-provided visual
reference; the reference video/screenshots were not imported. No upstream
video/character copyright ownership or exclusive rights are asserted.
Generated design token XML retains external source version/SHA metadata only.
React, ReactDOM, esbuild and Ajv retain MIT notices; app-kit downloads public
packages on demand into ignored paths instead of importing installed runtimes.
Codex runtime binary is not bundled; official Codex is Apache-2.0:
https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/LICENSE
Public AOSP test keys are fetched on demand for development only, never imported
from the user's existing signing cache and never used as production identity.

Taku Memory uses commonmark-java 0.30.1 (BSD-2-Clause). The build downloads
the parser from Maven Central and checks the SHA-256 in
system/assistant/markdown-dependencies.json. The parser's license ships in
system/memory/assets/licenses/commonmark.txt.

Native GenUI uses the Kotlin standard library (Apache-2.0), developed by the
Kotlin Team at JetBrains. Its upstream license and notice are packaged in the
assistant APK and task-broker JAR from system/assistant/assets/licenses/Kotlin-*.
https://github.com/JetBrains/kotlin

Magpie 0.1.2204 is MIT licensed by Yetone. Its official Android ARM64 program
is fetched by checksum into an ignored download cache and installed by the
development image. See adapters/magpie-runtime/LICENSE and
https://github.com/yetone/magpie/tree/v0.1.2204 . The MIT notice is installed
at /system_ext/etc/magpie-LICENSE. Provider credentials are device data,
never source files or image assets.

